# NOT .github/ — workflows must be IN the repo to run. The rule used to be
# here, and it was a trap of the same kind as the unanchored `build/` that
# once ate src/tools/build/: ci.yml and docs.yml survive only because they
# predate it, and any NEW workflow file would have been silently untracked —
# added, apparently committed, and never executed by anything.

# Kits (separate repos) + example game projects which not part of the engine repo
Kits/
fps_shooter/

# Compiled tool binaries (sources live in tools/)
fbx_diag

# ImGui window layout, rewritten on every panel move
imgui.ini

# macOS custom-folder-icon file; its name ends in a carriage return, so the
# `?` is a single-character wildcard rather than punctuation.
Icon?

# Rust build output. Cargo's own target dir (from a bare `cargo test` inside a
# crate) and the CMake-driven one (CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<build>/rust).
#
# ONE RULE PER CRATE, listed explicitly rather than a bare `target/`: this repo
# has a `src/render/pipeline/` and other directories where a future `target/`
# would be source, and a blanket pattern that hides real files is the failure
# 82e18cc had to undo for workflows. Add a line when you add a crate — the cost
# of forgetting is 17 MB of build output in a commit, which is what
# tests/audio_conformance/ was one `git add -A` away from.
modules/net/target/
tests/audio_conformance/target/
tests/cooked_format/target/
tests/module_abi/target/
